# Little owl

The little owl is a small, flat-headed predator of open country across Europe,
north Africa and temperate Asia. Unlike most of its family it is often abroad in
daylight, but the bulk of its foraging is done in the dark hours after dusk,
when it takes insects, earthworms and small rodents. It was introduced to
Britain in the nineteenth century and is now established across lowland England.
See [[strigidae]].
